Description: log the duration and size of each accesslog purge (2.6 backport)
 accesslog_purge() in 2.7 ends with a summary line under LDAP_DEBUG_SYNC:
 .
   accesslog_purge: dn="<suffix>" etime=<s>.<us> nentries=<n>
 .
 It is the only record of how long a purge took and how many entries it
 deleted. 2.6.x emits nothing at all, so on a 2.6 server running at the sync
 log level a purge is invisible: its duration and its delete rate can only be
 inferred from sampling something else, and a purge that takes tens of seconds
 is shorter than a comfortable sampling interval.
 .
 Both quantities are needed to size a purge schedule. The purge holds the
 accesslog environment's single writer for its whole duration, so the duration
 bounds how long a provider can be blocked, and the delete rate decides whether
 a given interval can keep up with the write rate at all.
 .
 This backports that block unchanged from 2.7.1, together with the one
 assignment it depends on: 2.7 sets op->o_qtime at the start of the purge and
 derives the age cutoff from it, while 2.6 derives the cutoff from
 slap_get_time(). Only the timestamp is added here; the cutoff arithmetic is
 left exactly as 2.6 has it, so the purge selects the same entries as before.
 .
 Nothing is emitted below LDAP_DEBUG_SYNC, which is where 2.7 puts it.
Forwarded: no
Author: Dominik Epple <dominik.epple@gmail.com>
Last-Update: 2026-10-20
---
--- a/servers/slapd/overlays/accesslog.c
+++ b/servers/slapd/overlays/accesslog.c
@@ -716,6 +716,7 @@
 	ava.aa_value.bv_val = timebuf;
 	ava.aa_value.bv_len = sizeof(timebuf);
 
+	gettimeofday( &op->o_qtime, NULL );
 	old -= li->li_age;
 	slap_timestamp( &old, &ava.aa_value );
 
@@ -792,6 +793,20 @@
 		ch_free( pd.dn );
 	}
 
+	if ( LogTest( LDAP_DEBUG_SYNC ) ) {
+		struct timeval now;
+		gettimeofday( &now, NULL );
+		now.tv_sec -= op->o_qtime.tv_sec;
+		now.tv_usec -= op->o_qtime.tv_usec;
+		if ( now.tv_usec < 0 ) {
+			--now.tv_sec; now.tv_usec += 1000000;
+		}
+		Debug( LDAP_DEBUG_SYNC, "accesslog_purge: "
+				"dn=\"%s\" etime=%d.%06d nentries=%d\n",
+				li->li_db->be_suffix[0].bv_val,
+				(int)now.tv_sec, (int)now.tv_usec, pd.used );
+	}
+
 	ldap_pvt_thread_mutex_lock( &slapd_rq.rq_mutex );
 	ldap_pvt_runqueue_stoptask( &slapd_rq, rtask );
 	ldap_pvt_thread_mutex_unlock( &slapd_rq.rq_mutex );
